//    CSS rotate(45deg) gives exactly that: in a y-down space the top end swings
//    right and up, the bottom end left and down.
//  • The tick's CENTRE snaps to the intersection, hence translate(-50%,-50%) —
//    it must straddle the dimension line, not hang off one side.
//  • Heavier than the lines it crosses (--dim-tick-w vs --dim-line-w) so the
