// A dashed extension / leader line. ONE definition, because five sites draw one and
// three things about it have to agree: the pen weight, the dash rhythm, and the
// markers the SVG exporter needs to find it (it has neither a border nor a
// background colour to recognise — see the .dim-dash-* rules in style.css).
//
// NO `opacity` on these any more. They carried 0.7, which NEITHER export honoured
// (emitEl doesn't read element opacity, so the SVG and the PDF always drew them at
// full strength) — so the editor was showing something softer than it would print.
// It also stacked with the anti-aliasing of a fractionally-positioned hairline and
// took some of them below the threshold of being visible at all. Drafting
// convention agrees: an extension line is the same weight and ink as the dimension
// line it serves. If they ever want softening again it has to reach all three.
//
// `dir` is 'v' for a line running down the page, 'h' for across. The caller sets
